Package: mysterynpi
Title: Name Keys and Agreement Rules for Linking Person Rosters to NPI
Version: 0.7.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Tyler", "Muffly", email = "tyler.muffly@dhha.org",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: One definition of the name-handling a provider linkage needs:
    transliterating join keys, given/middle/surname tokenisation, and the
    agreement rules that decide whether two records name the same person.
    Every rule here encodes a defect that has already shipped in a real
    pipeline, and each ships with the test that catches its return. The
    package provides governed blocking-key construction but deliberately
    stops short of dataset-specific candidate-generation policy and blended
    scoring: which blocking plans to deploy and what a study claims from the
    resulting evidence are pipeline science, not shared machinery.
